+++ b/docs/ONNX_RUNTIME.md
@@
+# Reduced ONNX Runtime for the browser
+
+The published opponent stays in **ONNX format** (`web/public/model.onnx`).
+The size reduction is in the WebAssembly execution runtime, not in a change to
+the model format.
+
+`web/runtime/` is built from the matching ONNX Runtime **v1.29.0** source with
+`--include_ops_by_config`. `reduced-ops.config` is generated directly from the
+published ONNX model, so unused operator kernels are omitted while normal ONNX
+loading remains available. This deliberately does **not** use `--minimal_build`,
+because ONNX Runtime's minimal Web build requires ORT-format models.
+
+The production Vite build selects onnxruntime-web's external-WASM JavaScript
+bundle. That prevents the package's generic WASM from being emitted alongside
+the reduced runtime. `copy-runtime.mjs` verifies `model.sha256` before copying
+the runtime; changing the network without rebuilding its operator set therefore
+fails the build rather than producing a broken Trained opponent.
+
+The real-browser regression suite loads the published model through this reduced
+runtime, including after an offline browser restart. `runtime-package.test.js`
+also fails if a generic hashed ORT WASM appears in `dist/assets` or if the reduced
+runtime is not smaller than the package runtime.
